{"content":[{"c":["ABIJAM"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Rehoboam’s son and successor as king of Judah, 913–910 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"}," (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.3.10","r":"1Chr.3.10","rawR":"1Chr.3.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.3.10","value":"1Chr.3.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 3:10"},"; alternately called “Abijah” in ",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.11.18-22","r":"2Chr.11.18-22","rawR":"2Chr.11.18-22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.11.18-22","value":"2Chr.11.18-22"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 11:18-22"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.12.16","r":"2Chr.12.16","rawR":"2Chr.12.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.12.16","value":"2Chr.12.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"12:16"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.13.1-22","r":"2Chr.13.1-22","rawR":"2Chr.13.1-22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.13.1-22","value":"2Chr.13.1-22"}],"t":"ref","v":"13:1-22"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.14.1","r":"2Chr.14.1","rawR":"2Chr.14.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.14.1","value":"2Chr.14.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"14:1"},"). A major focus of Abijam’s reign was his war with King Jeroboam I of Israel (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.13.1-3","r":"2Chr.13.1-3","rawR":"2Chr.13.1-3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.13.1-3","value":"2Chr.13.1-3"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 13:1-3"},"). Before a decisive battle, Abijam stood on Mt Zemaraim and shouted condemnation of Jeroboam’s political divisiveness and religious idolatry (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.13.4-12","r":"2Chr.13.4-12","rawR":"2Chr.13.4-12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.13.4-12","value":"2Chr.13.4-12"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 13:4-12"},"). Abijam and his army then prayed for God’s help in their precarious military position. Against two-to-one odds, they fought their way out of an ambush and won a stunning victory over Jeroboam (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.13.13-19","r":"2Chr.13.13-19","rawR":"2Chr.13.13-19","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.13.13-19","value":"2Chr.13.13-19"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 13:13-19"},"). Abijam’s reign in the southern kingdom of Judah was summed up rather unfavorably in ",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.15.1-8","r":"1Kgs.15.1-8","rawR":"1Kgs.15.1-8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.15.1-8","value":"1Kgs.15.1-8"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kings 15:1-8"},": “He committed the same sins as his father before him, and his heart was not right with the ",{"c":["Lord"],"sourceClass":"divine-name","t":"span"}," his God, as the heart of his ancestor David had been” (v ",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.15.3","r":"1Kgs.15.3","rawR":"1Kgs.15.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.15.3","value":"1Kgs.15.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"3"},", ",{"c":["nlt"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},"). But God had promised to keep David’s descendants on the throne in Jerusalem (",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.11.36","r":"1Kgs.11.36","rawR":"1Kgs.11.36","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.11.36","value":"1Kgs.11.36"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 11:36"},"), so Abijam’s son Asa succeeded him. Being of David’s line, Abijam was an ancestor of Jesus, the Christ (",{"href":"?bref=Matt.1.7","r":"Matt.1.7","rawR":"Matt.1.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.1.7","value":"Matt.1.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mt 1:7"},", “Abijah”)."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=IsraelHistoryof_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"IsraelHistoryof_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"IsraelHistoryof_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Israel, History of"},"; ",{"href":"?item=ChronologyoftheBibleOldTestament_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"ChronologyoftheBibleOldTestament_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"ChronologyoftheBibleOldTestament_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Chronology of the Bible (Old Testament)"},"; ",{"href":"?item=GenealogyofJesusChrist_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"GenealogyofJesusChrist_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"GenealogyofJesusChrist_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Genealogy of Jesus Christ"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Abijam","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"1 Chr 3:10","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.3.10","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.3.10","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.3.10"},{"anchorText":"2 Chr 11:18-22","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Chr.11.18-22","rawQueryValue":"2Chr.11.18-22","sourceRefExact":"2Chr.11.18-22"},{"anchorText":"12:16","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Chr.12.16","rawQueryValue":"2Chr.12.16","sourceRefExact":"2Chr.12.16"},{"anchorText":"13:1-22","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Chr.13.1-22","rawQueryValue":"2Chr.13.1-22","sourceRefExact":"2Chr.13.1-22"},{"anchorText":"14:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Chr.14.1","rawQueryValue":"2Chr.14.1","sourceRefExact":"2Chr.14.1"},{"anchorText":"2 Chr 13:1-3","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Chr.13.1-3","rawQueryValue":"2Chr.13.1-3","sourceRefExact":"2Chr.13.1-3"},{"anchorText":"2 Chr 13:4-12","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Chr.13.4-12","rawQueryValue":"2Chr.13.4-12","sourceRefExact":"2Chr.13.4-12"},{"anchorText":"2 Chr 13:13-19","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Chr.13.13-19","rawQueryValue":"2Chr.13.13-19","sourceRefExact":"2Chr.13.13-19"},{"anchorText":"1 Kings 15:1-8","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Kgs.15.1-8","rawQueryValue":"1Kgs.15.1-8","sourceRefExact":"1Kgs.15.1-8"},{"anchorText":"3","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Kgs.15.3","rawQueryValue":"1Kgs.15.3","sourceRefExact":"1Kgs.15.3"},{"anchorText":"1 Kgs 11:36","canonicalization":"deferred_to_d